{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"862901257383837716","content":"<@!150319814836092928> <@!340062533304057857>  *A 10 year old girl dressed in grubby clothes, a gatsby cap, and a satchel of papers slung around her shoulder catches up to you in the streets, and tells you the paper boss wants to see you.*\n\n*When you arrive at the Post, you wait for a few long minutes before the editor, Mr. Boch descends the stairs from his office on the second floor.*\n\"Thank you for seeing me this morning, both of you. I'll cut right to the chase. It seems you both witnessed the same event last night. I *could* just choose one of your articles to print, but I hate to see good talent go to waste. Instead, let me offer a solution. One of you, submit an accurate account of incident. What you both have written here is printable as-is, but maybe you could punch up the descriptions a bit. Readers love sensationalism. The other person should give a follow up commentary. Get some local reactions, maybe a statement from the Redcoats. Really play up the injustice of it all.\"\n\n\"I know a reporter's work is their pride and joy, but if the two of you can collaborate to get me two articles, one to print in tomorrow's paper, and one to print on the 14th, I'll throw in an extra 500 silver for each of you. I'll need both articles by 9pm tonight. What do you say?\"","created_at":"2021-07-12T13:47:39.570000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864140958925193216","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
